[h2]Killfeed[/h2]
The addon provides four combat displays plus a killcam. It credits players and AI and can identify the operator of a UAV or UGV.

[list]
[*][b]Killfeed[/b] lists recent eliminations and their causes. The server can change how long a line stays up, how many lines appear, which side of the entry the killer appears on and whether to mark AI.
[*][b]Midfeed[/b] shows your own eliminations and, if enabled, assists. The server controls its line limit, duration and whether “You” is highlighted.
[*][b]Deathfeed[/b] shows who hit you and how you died. The server can show or hide the report independently of the death transition.
[*][b]Kill-info[/b] shows the match records for everyone: longest kill and most kills in a row. The mission can show the records at round end. The server controls the display duration and whether team kills count.
[*][b]Killcam[/b] moves toward the player or unit that killed you. Press [b]Space[/b] to skip the killcam. The server can set its duration, maximum distance and aircraft altitude limit. It can also require a clear line of sight and choose whether to show it for team kills or indirect kills.
[/list]

Server options also control the assist window, friendly-fire messages, headshot and bullet icons, and whether a feed entry shows several damage causes. Players can turn off the killfeed, midfeed, deathfeed or killcam for themselves in the Client tab.

[h2]How to enable it[/h2]
In Eden, place the [b]Killfeed[/b] module to use it in that scenario. Enable it without an Eden module through [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=450814997]CBA_A3[/url]. Open [b]Addon Options → Killfeed[/b], check [b]Enable Killfeed[/b] and restart the mission. In multiplayer, use the Server tab.

